{{!--
  career-profile.md.hbs — renders CareerProfile (career-profile.schema.json)
  into the file the person owns and edits (mvp-spec §3 F5). Section order
  and headings below are exact, per the P01 packet spec.

  Render context (mostly a view-model derived from CareerProfile — the
  renderer, not this template, partitions `claims[]` by status.
  `presentation`/`boundaries`/`preferences` are direct passthroughs of the
  identically-shaped `ProfileStatement[]` schema fields, no partitioning
  needed):
    {
      profileVersion: number | null,   // approval.version, or null if never approved
      approvedAt: string | null,       // approval.at (ISO-8601), or null
      confirmedClaims:      [{ id, text, kind, source }],
      presentation:         [{ id, text }], // CareerProfile.presentation — profile-level wording rules ("Emphasise backend work for infrastructure roles"), never a claim or a claim status (P01 revision decision (a))
      needsDecisionClaims:  [{ id, text, kind, question }], // status: candidate | disputed, with an open question
      excludedClaims:       [{ id, text, kind }],
      boundaries:  [{ id, text }],
      preferences: [{ id, text }],
    }

  Every claim/boundary/preference/presentation line carries its `id` in
  brackets so editing this Markdown and re-parsing it round-trips into
  career-profile.json (F5 accept: "round-trip property test") — P03 owns
  the parser.
--}}
